{
 "_comment": "The runtime modules this editor loads, pinned by release tag and sha256 (scripts/modules.ts fetches and checks them into build/modules/<set>, nothing of a module's source is in this repository). Four sets, one loader. The two FF sets pin the re-issued releases engines-v1.2.1 and effects-v1.0.1 (the .wasm files are byte identical to the first releases, only the manifests changed). engines-os and effects-os: the public OpenTracker ports (ten synth engines, five master inserts), tag_status published: their GitHub release holds every file listed here and scripts/modules.ts without --from downloads it. engines and effects: the FF modules (PHZ and PLK, Console and Tube), proprietary freeware, built modules only. Their repository is not named here: repo_env names the environment variable that holds it (owner/name), scripts/modules.ts reads it, and a set whose variable is unset or unreadable is left out with --optional. Local stand-ins for --from (from_dir and also_from, directories with the same files, the first copy with the pinned sha256 wins) live in the git ignored modules.local.json, a map from set name to those two keys. engines.overrides: a module of the set that is not the tag's (PLK 1.1, see there). Regenerate the hashes with bun scripts/modules.ts --update --from.",
